      "math_academy_id": "e-3501",
      "problem": "What is the equation of the transformed sine curve shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/c7fa139446806a55084f05d99a4a33749ce789c5501b4136f602b4c7fec76a09.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\sin x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/8d97f8b2391f486572c1eecfb227d546d5af7d3950c96d2b9336d21608878e05.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\sin x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $1$ unit **right.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y = \\sin\\left(x-1\\right).$",
